Defines the types of warehouse operations (Receipts, Deliveries, Internal Transfers, Manufacturing, etc.) and controls their behavior, default locations, sequences, and routing rules.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Configure Incoming Receipts (from suppliers)
Configure Outgoing Deliveries (to customers)
Internal Transfers and inter-warehouse movements
Manufacturing / Production operations
Returns, Scrap, Inventory Adjustments
Multi-step processes (2-step / 3-step receipt & delivery)
Barcode operations and putaway strategies per type

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent)
Key Fields:
name (char, required), sequence_code (e.g. WH/IN, WH/OUT)
code (incoming/outgoing/internal/manufacturing)
warehouse_id → stock.warehouse
default_location_src_id, default_location_dest_id
sequence_id → ir.sequence
use_create_lots, use_existing_lots, show_entire_packs
reservation_method, auto_confirm, auto_assign
return_picking_type_id

Critical Hooks: onchange_warehouse_id, _get_action_picking_tree, routing engine integration
Security: stock.group_stock_manager + warehouse/company rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
operation type, picking type, stock.picking.type, warehouse operation, receipt type, delivery type, internal transfer type, WH/IN, WH/OUT, picking sequence, receipt operation, delivery operation
Related Models (most joined):

stock.picking (via picking_type_id — most important)
stock.warehouse
stock.location (default src/dest)
stock.rule (routes)
stock.move
ir.sequence

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
stock.picking.type is Odoo’s configuration model that defines warehouse operation types (Receipts, Deliveries, Internal, Manufacturing) with code, default locations, sequences, and behavior settings. It controls how stock.picking documents are created, numbered, and processed, and serves as the central configuration hub for all inventory movements, multi-step routes, and warehouse processes.